WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.803
Anthropic: Dario Amodei’s essays, 2024 to 2026.

2
00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:14.125
Anthropic’s CEO has written three long essays that together form the most detailed public timeline argument from a lab leader.

3
00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:34.565
“Machines of Loving Grace” (October 2024) defines “powerful AI”: a model smarter than Nobel Prize winners across most relevant fields, able to use computer interfaces, work autonomously on tasks lasting hours to weeks, and run as millions of copies at many times human speed.

4
00:00:34.845 --> 00:00:43.336
He calls this a country of geniuses in a datacenter and says it could arrive as early as 2026, while noting it could take much longer.

5
00:00:43.616 --> 00:00:58.464
The essay’s optimistic core is that such systems could compress 50 to 100 years of progress in biology and medicine into 5 to 10 years, limited by experiments, physical constraints, and regulation rather than intelligence.

6
00:00:58.744 --> 00:01:04.611
“The Adolescence of Technology” (January 2026) is the risk counterpart.

7
00:01:04.891 --> 00:01:22.235
It repeats that powerful AI could be as little as one to two years away, while allowing that it could take considerably longer, and lays out five risk categories: autonomy (systems pursuing goals against human interests), misuse for mass-casualty attacks, misuse to seize power,

8
00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.864
economic disruption, and indirect destabilization.

9
00:01:26.144 --> 00:01:33.184
It includes the forecast that AI could disrupt half of entry-level white-collar jobs over one to five years.

10
00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:53.069
“We Must Pace the Frontier” (12 September 2026) argues that progress sped up from around mid-2026 because AI increasingly helps build the next generation of AI, cites the OpenAI and Hugging Face incident (week 3) as a warning, and proposes a three-step plan:

11
00:01:53.349 --> 00:02:01.328
embedded third-party evaluators, coordination among frontier companies in democracies, and broader international coordination.

12
00:02:01.608 --> 00:02:04.403
Anthropic committed unilaterally to the first step.

13
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:17.461
In a February 2026 interview with Dwarkesh Patel, embedded below, Amodei explained the scaling hypothesis behind these views and why he thinks the public underestimates how close the field is.
